---
// Terms of use for the NOC app and community, at /terms. Keep them in step
// with the app (community rules: lib/community-model.ts; NOC+: app/plus.tsx)
// and with the privacy policy; change the date at the top when they change.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/PolicySection.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../links';

const UPDATED = '11 November 2026';
const CONTACT = CONTACT_EMAIL;
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use — NEVERMADE OUTDOOR CLUB"
  description="The terms for using the NEVERMADE OUTDOOR CLUB app and community: your account, safety outdoors, the community rules, NOC+ and your rights."
>
  <article class="wrap policy">
    <a href="/" class="label back">← NEVERMADE OUTDOOR CLUB</a>
    <h1>Terms<br />of use</h1>
    <p class="label meta">The NEVERMADE OUTDOOR CLUB app · Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
    <p class="intro">
      These terms apply when you use the NEVERMADE OUTDOOR CLUB app (NOC) and its community. By creating an account
      you agree to them. They're written to be read: if anything is unclear, ask us. How we handle your data is in
      the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="sections">
      <Section index="01" title="Who we are">
        <p>
          NOC is run by Duncan Kersbergen in the Netherlands. Questions, requests or complaints:{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="02" title="Your account">
        <ul>
          <li>You need to be <strong>16 or older</strong> to use NOC.</li>
          <li>Use your own details, one account per person, and keep your password to yourself.</li>
          <li>You're responsible for what happens on your account. Tell us if you think someone else is using it.</li>
        </ul>
      </Section>

      <Section index="03" title="Outdoors, at your own risk">
        <p>
          NOC helps you find places, plan routes, record outings and chase your firsts. Whether an outing is safe for
          you is your call:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Check before you go:</strong> weather, daylight, terrain, your gear, your fitness and local rules.
            Turn back when it doesn't feel right.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Maps and routes can be wrong:</strong> paths close, distances and directions may be off, and GPS can
            be inaccurate, especially in forests, mountains and cities. Use your own judgement and signs on the ground.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Don't let the app distract you</strong> while you ride, run near traffic or move over difficult
            ground.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>In an emergency</strong>, call the local emergency number (112 in Europe). NOC is not an emergency
            or safety service.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Section>

      <Section index="04" title="The community">
        <p>Everyone who posts agrees to the community rules in the app. In short:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Be decent:</strong> no harassment, hate, threats or bullying.</li>
          <li><strong>Keep it real:</strong> share your own outings and words. No spam, scams, fake accounts or advertising.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep people safe:</strong> don't encourage dangerous behaviour, and don't share where someone else
            lives or will be without their consent.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Keep it clean:</strong> no nudity, sexual content or graphic violence.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can report and block anyone. Reports are reviewed within 24 hours. We remove content that breaks the
          rules, and people who break them repeatedly lose access to the community.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="05" title="Your content">
        <p>
          What you record and post stays yours. You give us permission to store it and show it to the people you
          choose, only to run NOC. You can delete an outing, post or comment at any time. Only post what you have the
          right to share.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="06" title="NOC+">
        <p>
          NOC+ is an optional membership with extras. For now there's a free 14-day trial, once per account; nothing
          is charged. When NOC+ can be bought, the price and what's included are shown in the app before you buy, and
          payment, renewal and cancellation run through your Apple account under Apple's terms. You keep everything
          you recorded when NOC+ ends.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="07" title="The app">
        <p>
          NOC is still being built. Features can change, and we can't promise the app is always available or free of
          errors. If you downloaded NOC from the App Store, Apple's Licensed Application End User License Agreement
          applies as well.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="08" title="Liability">
        <p>
          As far as the law allows, we're not liable for injury, loss or damage from outdoor activities, from relying
          on maps, routes or other information in NOC, or from the app being unavailable. Nothing in these terms
          limits liability that can't be limited by law, or your rights as a consumer.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="09" title="Ending">
        <p>
          You can stop at any time: delete your account in the app (Settings → Delete account). We can suspend or end
          an account that breaks these terms or the community rules.
        </p>
      </Section>

      <Section index="10" title="Changes and law">
        <p>
          If we change these terms, we update them here and change the date at the top; for important changes we'll
          also tell you in the app. Dutch law applies. If you're a consumer in another country, you keep the
          protection its law gives you, and you can go to the courts where you live.
        </p>
      </Section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-block: 48px 96px;
  }
  .back {
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 6px 0;
  }
  .back:hover {
    color: var(--ice);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 12vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 0.85;
  }
  .meta {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .intro {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .intro a {
    color: var(--orange);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .sections {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 44px;
  }
</style>
